        "recommendation": "Bind the term as a parameter instead of concatenating it (CWE-89), as `query` in src/db.ts expects (\"values go in `params`, never in `sql`\"): `query<UserRow>(\"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name LIKE $1 ORDER BY name LIMIT 50\", [\"%\" + term + \"%\"])`. Attack today: any session with the `support` role sends `GET /users/search?q=x' UNION SELECT id, password_hash FROM users --` (src/server.ts:12-18 only trims and checks the length, 2 to 100 characters, which fits the payload) and reads any column of any table the database user can see, or alters data, beyond the id and name the endpoint is meant to expose. Consider also escaping `%`, `_` and `\\` in the term so a search for them matches literally.",
